# Pinned tracebloc/data-ingestors commit the CLI's embedded schema (and, when
# the goldens drift job lands, the validator goldens) are synced from. CI
# checks against THIS ref, not a floating branch — so an unrelated upstream
# commit can't red every open CLI PR (backend#1009).
#
# To adopt upstream changes: bump this SHA, then run `scripts/sync-schema.sh`
# (and `scripts/sync-validator-goldens.sh` once its CI job exists) and commit
# the regenerated files together in one deliberate PR.
#
# Format: the first non-comment, non-blank line is the ref (a full commit SHA
# preferred; a branch name works but reintroduces floating drift).
#
# CURRENT PIN: data-ingestors develop after the backend#3076 merge (#555 squash),
# which completes the backend#1006 object_detection migration. The previous pin
# (8f89aece, 2026-07-14) sat a full contract VERSION behind: its layout.v1.json
# was v2 and its ingest.v1.json PREDATED backend#1006, so it still accepted a
# `csv`/`label` for object_detection — the stale schema the CLI validated
# against locally while the cluster ingestor rejected the same config (HTTP 400,
# OD ingest impossible). This pin adopts the intervening upstream in one
# deliberate re-vendor: layout contract v2 -> v4 (v3 `ordering` block,
# backend#1870; v4 OD manifest kind="none", backend#3076), the di#360 dataset
# alignment fields + `data_id` default flip (content_hash) in ingest.v1.json,
# and the backend#1006 OD carve-out: `csv`/`json` are REJECTED for OD, and
# `label` is dropped from OD's REQUIRED set (the schema still permits it; the
# ingestor derives the per-image label from the XML and ignores any `label`).
